From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: execmem: ignore NULL before address classification

The module loader frees every init memory region, including absent regions
represented by NULL. Return before decoding the address to preserve the
NULL-free contract. On EVA platforms whose cached-address classifier also
accepts NULL, passing it to free_phys() corrupts unrelated page metadata.
Both non-NULL free paths remain unchanged.

This depends on OpenWrt's 301-01 execmem hooks and 301-02 allocator.
It repairs that OpenWrt-specific implementation and introduces no
board-specific allocation or address-mapping policy.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenWrt-specific execmem override]
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---
 arch/mips/kernel/module.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/module.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/module.c
@@ -176,6 +176,10 @@ static inline bool is_phys_addr(void *pt
 /* Free memory returned from module_alloc */
 void arch_execmem_free(void *ptr)
 {
+	/* Absent module init regions must be a no-op, before address decoding. */
+	if (!ptr)
+		return;
+
 	if (is_phys_addr(ptr))
 		free_phys(ptr);
 	else
